<h1>debug &mdash; <%= @debug.story.title %></h1>
<p class="nav">
  <%= link_to "&larr; back to the game".html_safe, playthrough_path(@playthrough) %>
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; playthrough #<%= @playthrough.id %>
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <%= @debug.turns.size %> turns
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; a snapshot: reload after a turn to see the next one
</p>

<%# THE TURN HE JUST TOOK. Everything else on this page is background to it. %>
<h2>the turn you just took</h2>
<% if @debug.latest_turn %>
  <%= render "debug/turn", turn: @debug.latest_turn, now: true %>
<% else %>
  <p class="absent">(this playthrough has no scene yet &mdash; nothing has been played)</p>
<% end %>

<%# WHERE HE IS STANDING. The stub-then-realize shape is the heart of the
    design and almost entirely invisible while playing. %>
<h2>where you are standing</h2>
<% if (place = @debug.location) %>
  <div class="panel">
    <div class="fields">
      <div class="k">name</div>
      <div class="v">
        <%= place.name %>
        <span class="tag <%= place.detail_level %>"><%= place.detail_level %></span>
        <% if place.mobile? %><span class="tag mobile">mobile</span><% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="k">description</div>
      <div class="v"><%= debug_value(place.description, absent: place.stub? ? "not written YET — this is a stub, and walking in is what realizes it" : "missing, and this place is realized — Location validates it") %></div>

      <div class="k">lore</div>
      <div class="v"><%= debug_value(place.lore, absent: place.stub? ? "not written YET — a stub has neither description nor lore" : "missing, and this place is realized — Location validates it") %></div>

      <div class="k">teaser</div>
      <div class="v"><%= debug_value(place.teaser, absent: "none — the one line a neighbour named it with") %></div>

      <div class="k">last visit</div>
      <div class="v">
        <%= debug_time(place.last_protagonist_visit, absent: "never — the next arrival narrates as discovery") %>
        <% if place.last_protagonist_visit %>
          <span class="note">(<%= debug_minutes((place.time_since_last_visit(@debug.story_clock).to_f / 60).round(2)) %> of story time ago)</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="k">parent location</div>
      <div class="v"><%= debug_value(place.parent_location&.name, absent: "none — nothing sets containment yet") %></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>the ways out, in both directions</h3>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>exit</th><th>state</th><th>distance</th><th>method</th>
          <th>time to travel</th><th>minutes</th><th>return edge</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @debug.exits.each do |exit| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= exit.location.name %></td>
            <td><span class="tag <%= exit.location.detail_level %>"><%= exit.location.detail_level %></span></td>
            <td><%= debug_value(exit.out&.distance) %></td>
            <td><%= debug_value(exit.out&.travel_method) %></td>
            <td><%= debug_value(exit.out&.time_to_travel) %></td>
            <td><%= debug_value(exit.out && LocationConnection.travel_minutes(exit.out.distance, exit.out.travel_method)) %></td>
            <%# Connections are written in both directions from one answer, so a
                missing return edge is a defect and not a shape of the world. %>
            <td><%= exit.one_way? ? tag.span("MISSING — one-way", class: "warn") : "yes" %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <% if @debug.exits.empty? %>
          <tr><td colspan="7" class="absent">(no exits — the classifier will accept no move from here)</td></tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <p class="absent">(this playthrough is nowhere &mdash; current_location is nil)</p>
<% end %>

<%# THE CLOSED SET. `Gate the state, inform the prose, audit the difference` --
    this is the gate, and it is the one thing on this page the standing
    constraint is actually about. %>
<h2>what the classifier will accept next turn</h2>
<div class="panel">
  <p class="note">
    <%= @debug.candidate_enum.size %> answers are physically available to the model:
    <code><%= @debug.candidate_enum.map(&:inspect).join(", ") %></code>.
    Anything else it might say resolves to <code>nothing</code> and the turn
    falls through to Scene::Narrator.
  </p>

  <div class="fields">
    <div class="k">exits offered</div>
    <div class="v"><%= debug_value(@debug.candidate_exits.map(&:name).to_sentence.presence, absent: "none — no move can be classified from here") %></div>

    <div class="k">people offered</div>
    <div class="v"><%= debug_value(@debug.candidate_cast.map(&:fullname).to_sentence.presence, absent: "nobody — no talk can be classified here") %></div>

    <div class="k">intents</div>
    <div class="v"><code><%= Playthrough::IntentSchema::INTENTS.join(" · ") %></code> &mdash; only <code>move</code> and <code>talk</code> have a branch that acts</div>
  </div>

  <h3>the prompt as it would be built</h3>
  <p class="note">
    Reconstructed from records just now &mdash; nothing captures what was
    actually sent last turn. See <em>what is not recorded</em> at the bottom.
  </p>
  <pre><%= @debug.classifier_prompt %></pre>
</div>

<%# THE WORLD'S OWN CLOCK. When the town rearranges itself overnight this is
    where it shows, and nowhere else: WorldEvent is deliberately not a
    narration source, so the player is never told. %>
<h2>the world's clock</h2>
<div class="panel">
  <div class="fields">
    <div class="k">story started</div><div class="v"><%= debug_time(@debug.story.start_time) %></div>
    <div class="k">Story#clock</div>
    <div class="v"><%= debug_time(@debug.story_clock) %> <span class="note">MAX(scenes.story_timestamp) — the high-water mark across every playthrough</span></div>
    <div class="k">you are at</div>
    <div class="v"><%= debug_time(@debug.story_now) %> <span class="note">this playthrough's own last scene</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>mechanics</h3>
<div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>name</th><th>kind</th><th>cadence</th><th>last run</th><th>fires next</th><th>owed now</th><th>events</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @debug.mechanics.each do |entry| %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= entry.mechanic.name %></td>
          <td><%= entry.mechanic.kind %></td>
          <td><%= entry.mechanic.cadence %> <span class="note">(<%= entry.mechanic.interval_minutes %> min)</span></td>
          <td><%= debug_time(entry.mechanic.last_run_at, absent: "never run") %></td>
          <td><%= debug_time(entry.next_at) %></td>
          <%# Normally empty: Playthrough::Turn#play catches the world up before
              it reads the command, so a boundary sitting here is a night the
              world has not paid for yet. %>
          <td><%= entry.owed.any? ? tag.span("#{entry.owed.size} boundary/ies pending", class: "warn") : "none" %></td>
          <td><%= entry.events.size %></td>
        </tr>
        <%# The in-fiction reason on its own row: it is a paragraph, and inside
            the name column it squeezes every dated column into three lines. %>
        <tr><td colspan="7" class="note"><%= debug_value(entry.mechanic.description, absent: "no in-fiction reason given") %></td></tr>
      <% end %>
      <% if @debug.mechanics.empty? %>
        <tr><td colspan="7" class="absent">(this world has no mechanics — it does not move on its own)</td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h3>what the world did to itself</h3>
<div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>occurred at</th><th>mechanic</th><th>summary</th><th>places touched</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @debug.world_events.each do |event| %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= debug_time(event.occurred_at) %></td>
          <td><%= event.world_mechanic.name %></td>
          <td><%= event.summary %></td>
          <td><%= debug_value(event.locations.map(&:name).to_sentence.presence, absent: "none recorded") %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <% if @debug.world_events.empty? %>
        <tr><td colspan="4" class="absent">(nothing yet — no boundary has been crossed since this world was made)</td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# THE LOG. Everything before the current turn, newest first, so it reads away
    from the present rather than towards it. %>
<h2>earlier turns</h2>
<% if @debug.earlier_turns.empty? %>
  <p class="absent">(none &mdash; the turn above is the whole log)</p>
<% end %>
<% @debug.earlier_turns.each do |turn| %>
  <details>
    <summary>
      <%= debug_branch(turn.branch) %>
      <%= debug_time(turn.scene.story_timestamp) %>
      &middot; <%= turn.scene.location.name %>
      &middot; <%= truncate(turn.scene.summary.presence || turn.scene.description.to_s, length: 90) %>
    </summary>
    <div class="body"><%= render "debug/turn", turn: turn %></div>
  </details>
<% end %>

<%# THE DURABLE BACKGROUND. Available, and deliberately not competing with the
    turn: all of it is closed until asked for. %>
<h2>the background</h2>

<details>
  <summary>the story &mdash; <%= @debug.story.title %> (<%= @debug.story.genre %>)</summary>
  <div class="body">
    <div class="fields">
      <div class="k">id</div><div class="v"><%= @debug.story.id %></div>
      <div class="k">genre</div><div class="v"><%= debug_value(@debug.story.genre) %></div>
      <div class="k">protagonist</div>
      <div class="v"><%= debug_value(@debug.story.protagonist&.fullname, absent: "none — no character has is_protagonist set") %></div>
      <div class="k">opening scene</div>
      <% opening = @debug.story.opening_scene %>
      <div class="v"><%= debug_value(opening && "scene ##{opening.id} in #{opening.location.name}", absent: "none — this world predates opening arrivals; PlaythroughsController wrote a fallback") %></div>
      <div class="k">summary</div><div class="v"><%= debug_value(@debug.story.summary) %></div>
    </div>
    <h3>preface</h3>
    <%= debug_prose(@debug.story.preface) %>
  </div>
</details>

<details>
  <summary>the universe &mdash; <%= @debug.universe.races.size %> races, <%= Universe::AUDIENCE_FIELDS.size %> prompt audiences</summary>
  <div class="body">
    <p class="note">
      Nothing here reaches a prompt whole: `Universe#prompt_details` sends each
      audience only the fields it can use.
    </p>
    <div class="fields">
      <% %i[physics technology weapons geographies civilizations history economics politics religion].each do |field| %>
        <div class="k"><%= field %></div>
        <div class="v"><%= debug_value(@debug.universe.public_send(field)) %></div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <h3>races</h3>
    <div class="fields">
      <% @debug.universe.races.order(:id).each do |race| %>
        <div class="k"><%= race.name %></div>
        <div class="v"><%= debug_value(race.description) %></div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<details>
  <summary>the cast &mdash; <%= @debug.cast.size %> characters</summary>
  <div class="body">
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>name</th><th>race</th><th>age</th><th>sex</th><th>pronouns</th><th>role</th><th>personality</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% @debug.cast.each do |character| %>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <%= character.fullname %>
                <% if character.nickname.present? %><br><span class="note">"<%= character.nickname %>"</span><% end %>
              </td>
              <td><%= debug_value(character.race&.name) %></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(character.age) %></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(character.sex_label) %></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(character.sex.present? ? character.pronouns : nil) %></td>
              <td>
                <% if character.is_protagonist? %><span class="tag realized">protagonist</span><% end %>
                <% if character.is_companion? %><span class="tag">companion</span><% end %>
              </td>
              <td><%= truncate(character.personality.to_s, length: 160) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<details>
  <summary>the map &mdash; <%= @debug.realized_count %> realized, <%= @debug.stub_count %> stubs</summary>
  <div class="body">
    <p class="note">
      A stub is a name and a teaser, created the moment a neighbour named it as
      an exit. Walking into one is what writes it, once and never again.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>place</th><th>state</th><th>exits</th><th>last visit</th><th>teaser / description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% @debug.places.each do |candidate| %>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <%= candidate.name %>
                <% if candidate.mobile? %><span class="tag mobile">mobile</span><% end %>
                <% if candidate == @debug.location %><span class="tag here">you are here</span><% end %>
              </td>
              <td><span class="tag <%= candidate.detail_level %>"><%= candidate.detail_level %></span></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(candidate.connected_locations.map(&:name).to_sentence.presence, absent: "none — nothing leads out of here") %></td>
              <td><%= debug_time(candidate.last_protagonist_visit, absent: "never") %></td>
              <td><%= truncate((candidate.description.presence || candidate.teaser).to_s, length: 160) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<details>
  <summary>every conversation in this world &mdash; <%= @debug.interactions.size %></summary>
  <div class="body">
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>character</th><th>place</th><th>typed</th><th>action</th><th>felt before → after</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% @debug.interactions.each do |interaction| %>
            <tr>
              <td><%= interaction.character_name %></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(interaction.location&.name) %></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(interaction.user_input) %></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(interaction.action) %></td>
              <td><%= debug_value(interaction.pre_feeling) %> &rarr; <%= debug_value(interaction.post_feeling) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
          <% if @debug.interactions.empty? %>
            <tr><td colspan="5" class="absent">(nobody has spoken to anybody in this world)</td></tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<%# THE HONEST GAP. Where something is absent rather than empty, say so -- and
    that applies to the view itself as much as to any field on it. %>
<h2>what is not recorded</h2>
<div class="panel">
  <ul class="evidence">
    <li>
      <strong>Prompts, raw responses, token counts, and which model actually
      answered.</strong> Every agent builds a bare <code>RubyLLM::Chat</code>; the
      <code>chats</code> / <code>messages</code> / <code>tool_calls</code> tables exist and are
      wired with <code>acts_as_chat</code>, but nothing ever writes to them. Queued as
      <code>ta-chat-persist</code>; this page gains all of it for free when that lands.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The classifier's intent label.</strong> Decided in memory inside
      <code>Playthrough::Turn#play</code> and never stored. Every branch above is
      derived from the records the branch left behind &mdash; which is the half
      that governs the game, because the loop dispatches on the resolved record
      and not on the label.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What the player typed, on any turn that was not a
      conversation.</strong> Only <code>Interaction#user_input</code> keeps it; a
      <code>Scene</code> has no column for the input that produced it. That migration is
      <code>ta-api-iface</code>'s first outstanding item.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What changed between two visits to a room.</strong> The exits a
      player was actually shown are not recorded on the Scene, so a shuffle is
      visible in the audit trail above but not as a diff. That is
      <code>ta-arrival-diff</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anything live.</strong> This page is a snapshot of the records as
      they stood when it was rendered. Take a turn, then reload.
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
